# Test that named args are type-checked by try_clause Step 2b.
# A typed param called with wrong-type named arg should produce an error.
# This test uses ONLY named args (no positional), so the "no matching clause"
# error can ONLY come from Step 2b (named arg type checking). Verified adequate.
[
  greet: [fn@String [let name@String] [str "Hello, " name]]
  result: [greet name: 42]
]
=== error
no matching clause
